# Normalize the sign-extended byte to unsigned [0,255] before the match,
# matching memchr semantics and fillMemoryBytesWithValue (which stores the
# low 8 bits). Without this, a byte >= 128 loads as a negative Int8 and would
# never match a targetValue in [128,255] — so fill(0xC8) then find(200)
# would wrongly report "not found".
